  "result": "Excellent! The CSV export function is complete and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully added **`exportCsv(invoices)`** in `src/export.js` that exports invoices to CSV format with proper RFC 4180 CSV escaping.\n\n### Implementation Details\n\n**`exportCsv(invoices)`** returns a CSV string with:\n- **Header row**: `number,customer,issueDate,dueDate,status,subtotal,discount,vat,total,due`\n- **Data rows**: One invoice per line in the order given\n- **Customer lookup**: Uses `getCustomer()` to resolve customer names from IDs\n- **Amount formatting**: Euros with 2 decimals and dot (e.g., `1234.50`) \u2014 no \u20ac sign, no thousands separator\n- **CSV escaping**:\n  - Fields containing commas or double quotes are wrapped in double quotes\n  - Double quotes inside fields are escaped by doubling them\n- **Line endings**: All lines end with `\\n`\n\n### Test Coverage\n\nAdded **21 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- \u2713 Empty invoice lists\n- \u2713 Single and multiple invoices\n- \u2713 Correct header and field count\n- \u2713 Customer name resolution\n- \u2713 Euro amount formatting (2 decimals)\n- \u2713 Order preservation\n- \u2713 Invoice statuses (draft, issued, partially_paid, paid)\n- \u2713 Payment states (unpaid, partially paid, fully paid)\n- \u2713 Discounts and VAT calculations\n- \u2713 Vouchers applied\n- \u2713 CSV escaping rules\n- \u2713 Line ending verification\n- \u2713 Amount precision\n\n**All 286 tests pass** across the entire project \u2713",
